<article>
	<h1><span>Storefront: Option</span></h1>

	<ul class="nav">
		<li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
		<li><a href="#fields">Fields</a></li>
		<li><a href="#toolbar">Toolbar</a></li>
	</ul>

	<section id="overview">
		<h2><span>Overview</span></h2>

		<p>This is where you can add a new option to an option group or edit an existing option.</p>
	</section>
	<section id="fields">
		<h2><span>Fields</span></h2>

		<h3>Details</h3>
		<dl>
			<dt>Title</dt>
			<dd>The name of the option. Required.</dd>
		</dl>

		<p>The right-hand column shows:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>ID</dt>
			<dd>The identification number of the option, assigned by the system. It cannot be changed.</dd>

			<dt>Option Group</dt>
			<dd>The name of the option group the option belongs to. It cannot be changed here.</dd>
		</dl>

		<h3>Parameters</h3>
		<dl>
			<dt>Publish</dt>
			<dd>Unpublished or Published.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="toolbar">
		<h2><span>Toolbar</span></h2>
		<p>At the top right you will see the toolbar.</p>
		<p>The functions are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Save</dt>
			<dd>Saves the option and stays on this screen.</dd>

			<dt>Save &amp; Close</dt>
			<dd>Saves the option and returns to the list of options of its option group.</dd>

			<dt>Cancel</dt>
			<dd>Discards any changes and returns to the list of options of its option group.</dd>

			<dt>Help</dt>
			<dd>Opens this help screen.</dd>
		</dl>
		<p>Save and Save &amp; Close only appear if you may edit products.</p>
	</section>
</article>
